<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahr Yusuf</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bahr Yusuf ('waterway of Joseph') is a channel that branches from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-egypt">Middle Egypt</a> and flows into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faiyum">Faiyum</a> depression. Kings of the Twelfth Dynasty, especially <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senusret-ii">Senusret II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenemhat-iii">Amenemhat III</a>, controlled its waters to reclaim land and extend cultivation in the Faiyum. It still waters the Faiyum's fields today.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bahr-yusuf.jpg" alt="Bahr Yusuf" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: مصطفي ابوبكر · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A8%D8%AD%D8%B1_%D9%8A%D9%88%D8%B3%D9%81_%D8%A8%D9%85%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%86%D9%8A%D8%A7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
